faqs:
  - q: "Is Squarespace a good choice for a law firm website?"
    a: "Yes, for most solo attorneys and small firms. Squarespace handles hosting and security for you, and you can update your own text and photos without hiring a developer. If your firm needs something Squarespace can't do, I also build on WordPress."
  - q: "Do you write the disclaimer and privacy policy?"
    a: "I set up the pages and make sure they're easy to find, including a short note on your contact form. The legal wording comes from you or your firm."
  - q: "Can you make my website accessible?"
    a: "I include accessibility basics on every site I build: readable text sizes, strong color contrast, image descriptions, clear headings and a contact form that works with a keyboard. I can also fix these on a site you already have, at $150/hr. For a full audit with screen reader testing, I recommend an accessibility specialist."
  - q: "How long does it take?"
    a: "A Website-in-a-Day is up in one day, once your text and photos are ready. A Custom Website takes about 3 to 4 weeks."
  - q: "Can you help my firm get more clients from Google?"
    a: "Yes. I also do SEO and Google Ads. You can see what's included and the prices on my <a href=\"/services#q-market\">services page</a>."
  - q: "Do you work with firms outside California?"
    a: "Yes. I'm based in Monterey, California, and I work with businesses all over the US over Zoom."
